{
  "hitlcad": 2,
  "name": "handhold-fan",
  "backend": "build123d",
  "brief": {
    "title": "Hand-held ducted blower for dusting a desktop PC",
    "summary": "A small 3D-printed ducted fan (like an EDF) driven by a 750 W brushless motor. Air enters through a finger guard at the back, a printed impeller pushes it past straightening vanes that also hold the motor, and a converging nozzle turns it into a narrow jet. A pistol grip under the duct holds the ESC; a switch or throttle pot sits under the index finger and the power cable leaves through the grip's end cap.",
    "key_dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Motor (assumed)",
        "value": 36,
        "note": "Ø36 × 50 mm inrunner can, Ø5 mm shaft sticking out 15 mm, 4 × M3 on a Ø25 mm circle in the shaft face: change the motor_* parameters to your motor"
      },
      {
        "name": "Impeller",
        "value": 68,
        "note": "Ø68 mm, 7 flat blades, Ø30 mm hub"
      },
      {
        "name": "Duct bore",
        "value": 69.5,
        "note": "0.75 mm tip gap all round"
      },
      {
        "name": "Nozzle outlet",
        "value": 20,
        "note": "Ø20 mm jet"
      }
    ],
    "features": [
      "duct: printed intake-end down; the bore steps out behind the impeller into a shoulder that the motor mount sits on",
      "motor_mount: bulkhead, motor collar and 6 straightening vanes on a ring; prints flat with no supports; the motor bolts under it with 4 × M3 and stays open to the airflow behind for cooling. Fan thrust pushes it onto the shoulder; the nozzle spigot keeps it from sliding out",
      "impeller: printed hub-face down, flat blades at 50° to the rotation plane (printable without supports), M3 set-screw boss on the shaft",
      "intake_guard: finger guard (≤ 7 mm slots) that slips over the duct's intake end",
      "nozzle: plugs into the outlet; printed tip-down on a flat lip",
      "handle: pistol grip with ESC bay and a switch hole, bolted to a pad under the duct with 4 × M3 into heat-set inserts; grip_cap closes it with 2 × M3 and has a cable hole"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "The motor is a Ø36 × 50 mm inrunner (3650 class) with a Ø5 mm shaft; outrunners need a different mount",
      "Powered by an external 4–6 S battery or 24 V supply through a cable; ESC (60–80 A) and a servo tester / throttle pot in the grip",
      "Printed in PETG (PA/nylon is better for the impeller)"
    ],
    "open_questions": [
      "Exact motor: diameter, length, shaft diameter and length, mounting holes, inrunner or outrunner, KV?",
      "Battery or mains supply?"
    ]
  },
